===============================================================================
                           ezHBot v1.0b
                     Headless ezQuake Client
===============================================================================

DESCRIPTION
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ezHBot is a lightweight, fully headless modification of the ezQuake client
(based on version 3.6.9), designed to run in server environments
without X11/Wayland, graphics cards, or audio drivers.

Purpose:

  * Viewing demos to record a complete qconsole.log.
  * Automated tasks and server monitoring.
  * Running in VPS and GUI-less containers.

===============================================================================
TECHNICAL IMPLEMENTATION
===============================================================================

The original ezQuake is strictly tied to a graphics subsystem.

ezHBot implements the following:

  [OK] Graphics renderer fully removed (RENDERER_NULL)
  [OK] Renderer calls stubbed out
  [OK] Lightmaps generation disabled
  [OK] Missing models substitution implemented
  [OK] Crashes on custom model requests eliminated

===============================================================================
SYSTEM REQUIREMENTS
===============================================================================

OS:
  * Ubuntu 20.04+
  * Debian 11+
  * CentOS/RHEL 8+

Architecture:
  * x86_64

Dependencies:
  libcurl4
  glibc

===============================================================================
QUICK START
===============================================================================

Directory structure:

  /path/to/ezhbot/
  |
  +-- ezquake-linux-x86_64
  |
  +-- id1/
  |   +-- pak0.pak
  |   +-- pak1.pak
  |
  +-- fortress/
  |
  +-- qw/
  |   +-- autoexec.cfg
  |   +-- qconsole.log
  |
  +-- qwproxy/
      +-- qwfwd
      +-- qwfwd.cfg

===============================================================================
BOT CONFIGURATION
===============================================================================

File: qw/autoexec.cfg

  name "HeadlessBot"
  spectator 1
  cl_net_clientport 0

  setinfo prx <PROXY_IP>:<PROXY_PORT>
  connect <SERVER_IP>:<SERVER_PORT>

===============================================================================
LAUNCHING
===============================================================================

Launching the proxy:

  cd /path/to/ezhbot/qwproxy/
  ./qwfwd -ip <SERVER_IP> -port <SERVER_PORT> +exec qwfwd.cfg &

Launching the bot:

  cd /path/to/ezhbot/
  ./ezquake-linux-x86_64 -nolan -nomouse -nosound -condebug &

===============================================================================
TROUBLESHOOTING
===============================================================================

[!] Bot does not connect to the server

    Check the autoexec.cfg settings.
    Make sure the -noautoexec parameter is not being used.

[!] status=203/EXEC

    Check execution permissions:
      chmod +x ezquake-linux-x86_64
      chmod +x qwfwd

[!] status=217/USER

    The specified user does not exist in the system.

